<figure class="cache-figure" data-memory-budget>
 <p class="figure-title">The eviction limit and the host limit count different things</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>maxmemory <input type="range" min="512" max="1600" step="16" value="1024" data-limit aria-label="Illustrative maxmemory" /><output data-limit-value></output></label><label>Extra snapshot pages <input type="range" min="0" max="1024" step="16" value="0" data-cow aria-label="Illustrative copy-on-write memory" /><output data-cow-value></output></label></div>
 <p class="figure-note">All numbers are MiB. Fixed demand: 1,400 MiB of memory counted for eviction. The model has already evicted eligible keys to meet maxmemory.</p>
 <div class="memory-budget-row"><span>Eviction accounting</span><div class="memory-budget-track"><span class="memory-counted" data-counted-bar></span><i data-eviction-line></i></div><small data-counted-label></small></div>
 <div class="memory-budget-row"><span>Host requirement</span><div class="memory-budget-track" data-total-bar><span class="memory-counted" data-segment="counted"></span><span class="memory-buffers" data-segment="buffers"></span><span class="memory-resident" data-segment="residentExtra"></span><span class="memory-cow" data-segment="cow"></span><span class="memory-other" data-segment="other"></span><i class="memory-host-line"></i></div><small data-total-label></small></div>
 <p class="figure-note">Both bars: 0–3,072 MiB. Vertical markers: configured maxmemory above; 2,048 MiB host limit below.</p>
 <ul class="memory-budget-legend"><li><i class="memory-counted"></i><span data-counted-text></span></li><li><i class="memory-buffers"></i>128 excluded buffers</li><li><i class="memory-resident"></i>128 additional resident overhead</li><li><i class="memory-cow"></i><span data-cow-text></span></li><li><i class="memory-other"></i>256 other host use</li></ul>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>This is a deliberately partitioned capacity model, not an equation obtained by adding INFO fields. Buffer, resident-overhead and other-use amounts are invented fixed inputs. Real accounting, allocator retention, transient overshoot and host/container limits require measurement. Increasing snapshot copies does not make more key memory eligible for eviction.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import {memoryBudget} from '../../lib/caching/memory.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-memory-budget]').forEach(root=>{const limit=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-limit]')!,cow=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-cow]')!;const render=()=>{const s=memoryBudget(Number(limit.value),Number(cow.value));let left=0;for(const k of['counted','buffers','residentExtra','cow','other']){const el=root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-segment="${k}"]`)!;el.style.left=`${left/3072*100}%`;el.style.width=`${s[k]/3072*100}%`;left+=s[k];}root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-counted-bar]')!.style.width=`${s.counted/3072*100}%`;root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-eviction-line]')!.style.left=`${s.limit/3072*100}%`;for(const[k,v]of Object.entries({'limit-value':`${s.limit} MiB`,'cow-value':`${s.cow} MiB`,'counted-label':`${s.counted} counted`,'total-label':`${s.total} required`,'counted-text':`${s.counted} Redis counted`,'cow-text':`${s.cow} snapshot copies`}))root.querySelector(`[data-${k}]`)!.textContent=v;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=`${s.evicted} MiB of requested cache allocation has been evicted. Host requirement is ${s.total} MiB: ${s.total>s.hostLimit?`${s.total-s.hostLimit} MiB above the host limit, despite satisfying maxmemory`:s.total===s.hostLimit?'exactly at the host limit, with no remaining headroom':`${s.hostLimit-s.total} MiB below the host limit under these assumptions`}.`;};limit.oninput=render;cow.oninput=render;render();});
</script>
